ate": "25/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/grech-delia-slam-abela-denying-involvement.1015902", "id": "ZFUQeJMBvyT_ytpRPRQy", "lat": 36.0396266, "long": 14.2454507, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Karol Aquilina: \u2018Labour MPs are fraudsters and Adrian Delia is my friend'", "Date": "27/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/karol-aquilina-labour-mps-fraudsters-adrian-delia-friend.1016295", "id": "ilUQeJMBvyT_ytpRXBTQ", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "\u2018Resignations are not enough'...", "Date": "27/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Financing"], "url": "https://www.maltatoday.com.mt/news/interview/121508/resignations_are_not_enough", "id": "jFUQeJMBvyT_ytpRXhSl", "lat": 36.0467778, "long": 14.25825649123654, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Nationalist Party leader Bernard Grech and MP Adrian Delia marched onto St Luke's hospital grounds with reporters on Tuesday, in an impromptu tour of the dilapidated site. Grech invited the press to walk with him through the hospital's front gates after Times of Malta asked him whether he and his MPs would ask for permission to enter, so that reporters could see the hospital's state. Video: Karl Andrew Micallef. The PN leader agreed. People have a right to see how Steward Healthcare failed to invest anything into the hospital, despite receiving millions in taxpayer money to do so, he said.\"As a matter of fact, after the press conference is finished, I invite you all to bring your cameras with you and walk with us inside,\" he told reporters. Photo: Karl Andrew Micallef. And that is what he did. The stroll was clearly unscheduled, prompting security personnel at the gate to follow the PN leader, politely", "Date": "28/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Financing"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/watch-grech-delia-march-st-lukes-hospital-gates-reporters.1016472", "id": "mVUQeJMBvyT_ytpRZBSY", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Mexico finds yet more corruption in health regulatory agency", "Date": "15/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Medicines", "Regulation"], "url": "https://federalnewsnetwork.com/business-news/2023/02/mexico-finds-yet-more-corruption-in-health-regulatory-agency/", "id": "KVTvd5MBvyT_ytpRUtxX", "lat": 19.4326296, "long": -99.1331785, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Fraud"], "country": "Mexico", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Former Rush Hospital chief indicted", "Date": "15/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Financing"], "url": "https://wgntv.com/news/wgn-investigates/former-rush-hospital-chief-indicted/", "id": "Z1Twd5MBvyT_ytpRBd6q", "lat": 41.87891665, "long": -87.80307008250303, "Corruption Categories": ["Laundering proceeds of crime", "Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "W.H.O.: China Coronavirus Deaths 'Heavily Underreported'", "Date": "12/01/23", "Sector Categories": ["COVID-19"], "url": "https://www.breitbart.com/asia/2023/01/12/w-h-o-china-coronavirus-deaths-heavily-underreported-hurting-global-data/", "id": "BlTud5MBvyT_ytpRntpO", "lat": 39.9057136, "long": 116.3912972, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "China", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "NEET list forged in Uttar Pradesh: Ayurveda Dept ex-director, 14 others charged by Special Task Force", "Date": "16/02/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://medicaldialogues.in/news/education/ayush/neet-list-forged-in-uttar-pradesh-ayurveda-dept-ex-director-14-others-charged-by-special-task-force-107190", "id": "AVTwd5MBvyT_ytpR2-FI", "lat": 26.8381, "long": 80.9346001, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "India", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "They Have Lost Their Power To Scare The Non-Insane", "Date": "17/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["COVID-19"], "url": "https://www.truth11.com/war-of-the-worlds/", "id": "llTxd5MBvyT_ytpRIOHf", "lat": 36.1672559, "long": -115.148516, "Corruption Categories": [], "country": "United States", "f_n": true, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health", "Defence"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Beauticians at Spain clinic arrested after 'women injured by botched treatments'", "Date": "17/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery"], "url": "https://www.thesun.ie/news/10242879/costa-del-sol-clinic-arrested-skin-botched-treatments/", "id": "oFTxd5MBvyT_ytpRJOFK", "lat": 36.487587, "long": -4.9537861, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Spain", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Adrian Delia. His name elicits many different reactions. For those who know him, a heart of gold, sharp, hilarious at times, an ability to effortlessly empathise and adapt and a genuineness and authenticity that is endearing and that does him immense credit. For those who remember, an eventful PN leadership campaign, an even more eventful PN leadership period. He was strongly opposed by several within the party and the wider community, mostly on rumours, perceptions and prejudice, but not only. I too did not back him, strongly, and I will not and do not hide from it. Not personal, not prejudice and not blindly, but I did oppose him and a man should always own up to his actions. As childhood school friends we did not allow it to ruin a deep bond that runs through our veins and we more than spoke about it and understood each other. That, too, is what men should do. Disagreement and conflict is human and normal. So is debate, discussion and compromise, which lead to healing, understanding and an even stronger bond than ever before. Friday's judgment that annulled the infamous Vitals-Steward deal and that ordered the return of three hospitals to the public shocked the nation. The implications are very clear and the consequences should be inevitable. A greengrocer who failed to file VAT returns was sent to prison. Another greengrocer who ran a rather unorthodox, albeit insignificant scheme was also sent to prison. Logically, public officials at the time who have been found by the courts to have abusively used huge amounts of public tax monies on a hugely corrupt and criminally infested deal, should face the music. Their status as public officials further aggravates their crimes, as the criminal code clearly states. It is now in the hands of the competent authorities to drive that home \u2018without fear or favour'. This is meant to be a European democracy, so justice should be allowed to take its course, but there is a limit to patience and it is wearing very thin. We are nearing spring so the cracks on the ice are starting to develop. The competent authorities should understand that real equality is not only achieved by painting multicoloured zebra crossings, neutralising history and amending laws, commendable and necessary as they were. That is Adrian Delia at his finest. Sharp, intelligent, perceptive and determined",