obert-abela-joseph-muscat-tensions.1015998", "id": "LVUSeJMBvyT_ytpRtBso", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Assistant medical officer remanded over funeral arrangement graft probe", "Date": "08/02/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.nst.com.my/news/crime-courts/2023/02/877709/assistant-medical-officer-remanded-over-funeral-arrangement-graft", "id": "f1UUeJMBvyT_ytpROSHF", "lat": 3.7985637, "long": 103.32199, "Corruption Categories": [], "country": "Malaysia", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Misappropriation from CMDRF: Vigilance reports major irregularities, recommends action against officials", "Date": "24/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery", "Financing"], "url": "https://keralakaumudi.com/en/news/news.php?id=1014356", "id": "zVUUeJMBvyT_ytpRhyLr", "lat": 8.4882267, "long": 76.947551, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "India", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Doctors under investigation for taking medical devices from corpses and fitting them to patients", "Date": "17/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery"], "url": "https://www.romaniajournal.ro/society-people/health/doctors-under-investigation-for-taking-medical-devices-from-corpses-and-fitting-them-to-patients/", "id": "0lUUeJMBvyT_ytpRiSJ5", "lat": 45.6525105, "long": 25.6105654, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Romania", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Muscat's cabinet omerta' \u2013 Kevin Cassar", "Date": "28/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Regulation"], "url": "https://theshiftnews.com/2023/02/28/muscats-cabinet-omerta-kevin-cassar/", "id": "41UUeJMBvyT_ytpRjSKO", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": true, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Steward Health Care has questioned the outcome of a judgment annulling the controversial deal that handed over the running of three state hospitals to a private consortium, calling the statements made against it as 'outrageous and without merit'. Ruling on a case started by former PN leader Adrian Delia, Judge Francesco Depasquale said on Friday that the deal shepherded under former prime minister Joseph Muscat's administration was 'corrupt and fraudulent' and that the Gozo General Hospital, St Luke's Hospital and Karin Grech Hospital should be returned to the state because promised targets were never met. The judge also said that fraud was established in three stages of the process. But in a statement later on Friday, Steward Health Care, which currently holds the concession, said it 'strongly objects' to the outcome of the judgment and questioned the state of rule of law in Malta. The company said it is considering its position and reserved the right to safeguard its interests in both local and international courts. 'SHCM will pursue action contesting all allegations of wrongdoing raised in the court judgement, allegations we consider outrageous and without merit,' it said. Steward said that preliminary reviews of the judgment showed it contained 'significant flaws in reasoning'. 'We believe that the judgment, which goes far beyond the court's remit, presents major concerns for the rule of law in Malta and has serious implications for the future of foreign investment in the country.\" 'The legal, operational, and practical aspects of the consequences of the court's judgement need to be assessed in detail and understood thoroughly. SHCM remains committed to operate at all times in accordance with its highest professional standards and values.' The company said its priority remains in providing optimal healthcare to the communities and patients it is entrusted to serve. Independent journalism costs money. Support Times of Malta for the price of a coffee. Support Us", "Date": "24/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/outrageous-merit-steward-reacts-deal-annulment.1015848", "id": "zlUTeJMBvyT_ytpRVh0X", "lat": 36.0467778, "long": 14.25825649123654, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Watch: Robert Abela Should Now Scrap 'Corrupt' Electrogas Deal, Adrian Delia Says On Jon Mallia's Podcast", "Date": "25/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement"], "url": "https://lovinmalta.com/malta/watch-robert-abela-should-now-scrap-electrogas-deal-adrian-delia-says-on-jon-mallias-podcast/", "id": "iVUTeJMBvyT_ytpRgh6r", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Bar Ngatia's company from Sh10.2b tender, court urged", "Date": "28/02/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement"], "url": "https://www.pd.co.ke/news/bar-ngatias-company-from-sh10-2b-tender-court-urged-171155/", "id": "hVUUeJMBvyT_ytpRviPo", "lat": -1.3026148499999999, "long": 36.82884201813725, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Misappropriation"], "country": "Kenya", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Dozens of Americans die daily waiting for an organ transplant. Why do we let this happen?", "Date": "01/03/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2023/03/01/break-up-organ-donation-monopoly/11259464002/", "id": "alU-eJMBvyT_yt