 "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Finance director of Seattle nonprofits pleads guilty to embezzling $3 million", "Date": "18/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Financing"], "url": "https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/law-justice/finance-director-of-seattle-nonprofits-pleads-guilty-to-embezzling-3-million/?utm_source=RSS&utm_medium=Referral&utm_campaign=RSS_all", "id": "OVYReZMBvyT_ytpRDSvZ", "lat": 47.6038321, "long": -122.330062, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Other", "Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Nurses Protest against PPP, Cabinet for Presidential Veto of Nursing Act", "Date": "19/05/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "http://world.kbs.co.kr/service/news_view.htm?lang=e&Seq_Code=177920", "id": "1FYPeZMBvyT_ytpRfSSY", "lat": 37.5716162, "long": 126.9769026, "Corruption Categories": [], "country": "South Korea", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Patients suffer as strike at ATH enters 5th day", "Date": "30/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Financing"], "url": "https://www.thenews.com.pk/print/1075162-patients-suffer-as-strike-at-ath-enters-5th-day", "id": "i1YGeZMBvyT_ytpRFQwT", "lat": 34.204373149999995, "long": 73.23731878380386, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Pakistan", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "ATH staff boycotts duties till BoG chairman resignation", "Date": "25/05/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.thenews.com.pk/print/1073697-ath-staff-boycotts-duties-till-bog-chairman-resignation", "id": "mlYGeZMBvyT_ytpRjg7R", "lat": 34.1436136, "long": 73.2132747, "Corruption Categories": ["Nepotism/Cronyism/Favouritism"], "country": "Pakistan", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "PN general council president Mark Anthony Sammut has handed in 'new evidence' on the Vitals/ Steward hospitals deal to the inquiring magistrate investigating the case. Addressing a news conference that was also attended by party leader Bernard Grech and other PN MPs, Sammut said that he had received information directly from a person who knew of the deal's ongoings. 'This is the first time in this entire case that a person that has facts and was aware of what was happening moved forward to speak up and give their version of events about this deal,' he said on Thursday morning. Sammut said that the application filed in court includes sworn testimony from the unnamed source, copies of agreements, and correspondence between Vitals and Steward management and PL politicians, government officials and government consultants. 'The evidence indicates fraud, threats, false declarations, and collusion between politicians, high government officials and businessmen,' he said. 'I saw the evidence, I saw these documents and as an MP and as a citizen of this country I feel obliged to pass this information about the concession of these three hospitals to the inquiring magistrate,' Sammut said. Speaking in front of the law courts, he said his source is willing to testify directly in front of the inquiring magistrate who is currently conducting her criminal inquiry into the transfer of three hospitals. Vitals Global Healthcare (VGH) took control of St Luke's, Gozo General and Karin Grech hospitals in 2015 for a 30-year period, a contract that was later passed onto Steward Global Healthcare. The contract was nullified in court some weeks ago in a judgement that described the deal as fraudulent. New revelations by Times of Malta, The Shift and OCCRP show that the VGH people entrusted with running the hospitals had splurged cash on luxury cars, five-star hotels, private schools and even Netflix subscriptions, according to financial documents. The transactions fuel suspicions that the people involved in the deal had mismanaged public money. A corruption probe into former prime minister Joseph Muscat has also been combing through his bank accounts and income declarations for evidence of wrongdoing. Investigators suspect that one consultancy contract with Swiss company SpringX Media, which netted Muscat \u20ac60,000, could have been used as a vehicle to disguise payments from the deal in plain sight. SpringX Media shares the same address with Accutor Consulting. Research by Times of Malta shows how Accutor Consulting used to be called VGH Europe. On Thursday, PN leader Bernard Grech said that no matter how powerful, 'everyone, who has faltered should face justice'. He said prime minister Robert Abela is in a 'satanic pact' with Joseph Muscat and is doing all he can to protect the ex-prime minister. Grech said that two weeks have passed since the party submitted a report to the police asking them to investigate a slate of politicians, including Robert Abela about their involvement in the deal. 'The police commissioner still does not want to do anything about this,\" he said. Independent journalism costs money. Support Times of Malta for the price of a coffee. Support Us PREVIOUS Aston Martin Works widens availability of new parts for classic models NEXT Peter Paul Coleiro officially takes on role as head of CPD Comments Comments not loading? We recommend using Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox. Please enable JavaScript to view the comments powered by Disqus. Comments powered by Disqus", "Date": "18/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Financing"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/pn-files-new-evidence-hospitals-deal-court.1032311", "id": "9lYGeZMBvyT_ytpRpA58", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Baby selling racket exposed in Thane: Doctor arrested, nursing home shut down", "Date": "20/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery"], "url": "https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/baby-selling-racket-exposed-in-thane-doctor-arrested-nursing-home-shut-down", "id": "slYGeZMBvyT_ytpR1g-I", "lat": 19.186483, "long": 72.9757664, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "India", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Liberia: Corruption Allegations Against Jeremiah Koung as the Senator Becomes UP Vice Presidential Aspirant", "Date": "16/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Financing"], "url": "https://www.liberianobserver.com/liberia-corruption-allegations-against-jeremiah-koung-senator-becomes-vice-presidential-aspirant", "id": "G1YFeZMBvyT_ytpRNgr1", "lat": 6.328034, "long": -10.797788, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Misappropriation"], "country": "Liberia", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Democracy", "Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Zim: When bureaucracy fails", "Date": "13/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "COVID-19"], "url": "https://www.newsday.co.zw/opinion-analysis/article/200011463/zim-when-bureaucracy-fails", "id": "aVYFeZMBvyT_ytpRSQri", "lat": -17.831773, "long": 31.045686, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Zimbabwe", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Worldwide Bio-Warfare Exposed: David Martin Uncovers Covid as Act of Biological, Chemical Warfare at EU International Covid Summit", "Date": "26/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["COVID-19"], "url": "https://www.infowars.com/posts/worldwide-bio-warfare-exposed-david-martin-uncovers-covid-as-act-of-biological-chemical-warfare-at-eu-international-covid-summit", "id": "nVYTeZMBvyT_ytpRTS-g", "lat": 50.8465573, "long": 4.351697, "Corruption Categories": [], "country": "Belgium", "f_n": true, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Italian police nab 61 'Ndrangheta members", "Date": "11/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Service Delivery", "Financing"], "url": "https://www.poandpo.com/news/italian-police-nab-61-ndrangheta-members/", "id": "AFX-eJMBvyT_ytpRq_vZ", "lat": 38.6748544, "long": 16.0985276, "Corruption Categories": ["Extortion", "Bribery", "Laundering proceeds of crime", "Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Italy", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health", "Democracy"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Alleged gang members who \u2018sold Armenian babies' keep jobs", "Date": "31/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery", "Regulation"], "url": "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/armenia-italy-illegal-adoptions-work-government-hospitals-babies/", "id": "JlX-eJMBvyT_ytpRtfuY", "lat": 40.1777112, "long": 44.5126233, "Corruption Categories": ["Laundering proceeds of crime", "Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "Armenia", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Joseph Muscat has demanded that a magistrate leading a corruption probe into the hospitals deal step down immediately. In a judicial filing on Thursday, the ex-prime minister said he wants magistrate Gabriella Vella to step down from the inquiry and pass it on to someone else \"who can secure impartiality, both as perception and a matter of fact, in this case, which has now turned political\". Muscat has been under renewed scrutiny following revelations by Times of Malta and its media partners linking him to a Swiss firm that used to be called VGH Europe. He received \u20ac60,000 in suspicious Swiss payments that are being scrutinised by the inquiry. The corporate trail. Muscat's home was searched last year as part of the ongoing probe. The ex-prime minister complained on Facebook that the magistrate has yet to hear his version of events. \"For some reason, she was comfortable in ordering the police to enter on my family in our home but not in hearing what I have to say,\" Muscat complained. Muscat also claimed there have been \"continuous leaks\" in the inquiry, including people publicly boasting about knowing what was going to happen, and people turning up on his doorstep to follow proceedings. He further claimed that members of the magistrate's immediate family \"promote propaganda\" by those who filed the inquiry, a reference to rule-of-law NGO Repubblika. \"Constitutional case law, the code of ethics and international principles governing the judiciary are clear about this.\"I have resisted taking this step for some time to give the benefit of doubt but the outrageous moves of the past few days made me lose all possible trust I could have in this process,\" Muscat said. The ex-prime minister said he is ready to \"fight on my own for the truth to prevail and for those cooking up conjectures to suit their political agenda to pay\". Independent journalism costs money. Support Times of Malta for the price of a coffee. Support Us PREVIOUS Bernice Cassar's family seek to intervene in case challenging femicide law Comments Comments not loading? We recommend using Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox. Please enable JavaScript to view the comments powered by Disqus. Comments powered by Disqus", "Date": "18/05/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/joseph-muscat-wants-vitals-inquiry-magistrate-step.1032317", "id": "PFX-eJMBvyT_ytpRuvuV", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Tips surge after nurse practitioner charged with sex crimes", "Date": "06/05/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://nationalpost.com/pmn/news-pmn/tips-surge-after-nurse-pr