df31 Pain Clinic Kickbacks + Saturday Lake Drowning + Cars For The Band", "Date": "13/06/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery", "Financing"], "url": "https://patch.com/georgia/woodstock/pain-clinic-kickbacks-saturday-lake-drowning-cars-band", "id": "ClYreZMBvyT_ytpRlV9E", "lat": 34.1014112, "long": -84.5192192, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Baltimore mayor on furlough as book scandal deepens", "Date": "08/06/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://shepherdgazette.com/baltimore-mayor-on-furlough-as-book-scandal-deepens/", "id": "lVYjeZMBvyT_ytpRIlBK", "lat": 39.2908816, "long": -76.610759, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Coalition government's \u2018brazen' health grant breach \u2018worse than sports rorts', integrity body says", "Date": "07/06/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/jun/07/coalition-governments-brazen-health-grant-breach-worse-than-sports-rorts-integrity-body-says", "id": "llYxeZMBvyT_ytpRd2_R", "lat": -24.7761086, "long": 134.755, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation"], "country": "Australia", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": true}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Muscat in Smash TV interview: dog-whistle politics in the war against \u2018the freemasons'", "Date": "02/06/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.maltatoday.com.mt/news/national/123252/muscat_in_smash_tv_interview_dogwhistle_politics_in_the_war_against_the_freemasons", "id": "pVYxeZMBvyT_ytpRfG8X", "lat": 35.8989979, "long": 14.5136607, "Corruption Categories": [], "country": "Malta", "f_n": false, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Why Yogi govt is dragging its feet over CBI probe in Ayush scam?", "Date": "17/06/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "http://tehelka.com/why-yogi-govt-is-dragging-its-feet-over-cbi-probe-in-ayush-scam/", "id": "_1Y5eZMBvyT_ytpRjnuu", "lat": 26.8381, "long": 80.9346001, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "India", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Five IAS officers transferred in UP, ACS Finance Prashant Trivedi removed from the post, allegations are leveled in this matter", "Date": "01/06/23", "Sector Categories": [], "url": "https://www.weeklyblitz.net/news/five-ias-officers-transferred-in-up-acs-finance-prashant-trivedi-removed-from-the-post-allegations-are-leveled-in-this-matter/", "id": "FFY5eZMBvyT_ytpRz32b", "lat": 26.8381, "long": 80.9346001, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery"], "country": "India", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Brooklyn social worker who ditched special-needs kids in Medicaid scam gets 42 months in prison", "Date": "08/06/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery", "Financing"], "url": "https://www.nydailynews.com/new-york/nyc-crime/ny-social-worker-special-needs-children-fraud-sentence-20230608-tfoaht3rzjebbdwma56vtvznqm-story.html", "id": "eFYheZMBvyT_ytpRIEmR", "lat": 40.6526006, "long": -73.9497211, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Inside lavish life of FBI Most Wanted 'fraudster', who wriggled free", "Date": "26/06/23", "Sector Categories": ["Financing"], "url": "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-12210881/Inside-lavish-life-FBI-Wanted-fraudster-judges-let-wriggle-free.html", "id": "t1YheZMBvyT_ytpRMUl0", "lat": 26.4614625, "long": -80.0728201, "Corruption Categories": ["Misappropriation", "Fraud"], "country": "United States", "f_n": false, "c_n": true, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Design alternatives Rota.mt firmly believes that road-dieting can be an effective solution to address congestion problems but it must be implemented correctly. Simply removing a car lane is a half-baked solution if it does not change the car-centric nature of the road and fails at providing alternatives to driving in the gained space. Photo: Rota.mt In light of this, we would like to show an alternative approach to road-dieting in G\u0127adira. Here are two conceptual designs, by no means precise, sketching just one out of endless possible options at the narrowest width and at a typical width. Traffic lanes are retained in each direction but dedicated lanes for cyclists, pedestrians and other road-users seeking alternative transportation methods are incorporated. Big parking areas were built just nearby in recent years; therefore, unrestricted parking in such premium seafront should not be priority. This comprehensive plan ensures a balanced and efficient use of the road space, accommodating the needs of various users while alleviating congestion. Photo: Rota.mt It is not clear what route is intended for users cycling here to reach the \u010airkewwa ferry terminal, as there are no alternative ways available. Being the only road between Mellie\u0127a and the Torri l-A\u0127mar, a cycling path should be prioritised and not omitted. Juan Buhagiar Duijst, policy officer, Rota.mt \u2013 \u0126amrun Only in Malta Prime Minister Robert Abela recently attended the fourth summit of the European Union. This was just after he was handed the auditor general's report condemning him and the rest (too long to list) of negotiating the three hospital deals with Vital Global Healthcare and later Steward Health Care. First of all, it was he who declared he would be asking the auditor general to check how much money Vitals and Steward were given, after the court declared the deal fraudulent from its conception. Now, Abela cannot act like Pilate. He cannot wash his hands of this corrupt deal. Abela was legal advisor to Joseph Muscat who, besides being disgraced, is still happily availing himself and his wife of thousands of euros from our taxes. Abela also attended cabinet meetings, so when he moans about not knowing anything about the deal, he is only lying through his teeth. I remember him saying that, although being part of Muscat's cabinet, he didn't have a particular portfolio, like Chris Fearne and Ian Borg, but Muscat wanted him to have an overview of all ministries. Quite a vast responsibility, I dare say! Abela has been misleading the Maltese all along. The public is also wondering why Abela gave Muscat a diplomatic passport after he had been declared the most corrupt person for 2019. Shame on all. It's amazing how Abela has the cheek to mix with other dignitaries who, I am sure, are aware of his shady history. Emily Barbaro-Sant \u2013 Mosta Independent journalism costs money. Support Times of Malta for the price of a coffee. Support Us PREVIOUS School board head's firm made \u20ac3m from works over the years NEXT EU countries try to thrash out refugee burden-sharing Comments Comments not loading? We recommend using Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox. Please enable JavaScript to view the comments powered by Disqus. Comments powered by Disqus", "Date": "08/06/23", "Sector Categories": ["Procurement", "Financing", "Regulation"], "url": "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/letters-editor-june-8-2023.1036238", "id": "G1Y2eZMBvyT_ytpR2HU0", "lat": 7.06667, "long": 39.26667, "Corruption Categories": ["Bribery", "Misappropriation"], "country": "Malta", "f_n": true, "c_n": false, "Industry": ["Health"], "country_level": false}, {"Archived": false, "Title": "Florida, Alabama Men Charged in Separate Genetic Testing Fraud Schemes", "Date": "29/06/23", "Sector Categories": ["Service Delivery", "Financing"], "url": "https://